aming for granitemoe, mixtral/llama-MoE, qwen2moe/qwen3moe (shared expert, ffn_*_shexp), deepseek2 (MLA attn tensors), gpt-oss, and our hybrid-split `.hot`/`.cold` tensors; unknown tensors -> role \"other\" + listed (never silently dropped).\n - Optional `--trace` routing-trace input (format: read cc/routing_trace/README.md and its tools; experiments/routing/ has real outputs): per-layer expert frequency, entropy, Gini, coverage curve (fraction of routed requests covered by top-H experts, H=1..E), and recommended hot set size per layer for coverage targets 0.5/0.75/0.9 — with the trace's split/phase recorded and a warning that train≠eval.\n - CLI: `inspect_model.py <gguf> [--trace T] [--out stats.json] [--summary]` (summary = human table).\nTests (pytest): run on the REAL GGUFs in ~/models/campaign/gguf (bf16, Q8_0, Q4_K_M, mixE4K) — check expert share ≈ 90% of weight bytes for bf16 (decisions/D013), mixE4K experts Q4_K/rest Q8_0, and that the hybrid split file artifacts/codexR/models/granite-split-n12.gguf is recognized (hot/cold roles, null experts counted). Plus tiny synthetic GGUFs (write with gguf-py into tmp) for qwen3moe-with-shared-expert and deepseek2 naming.\nAllowed writes: cc/model_inspect/**, artifacts/codexMI/. 40 min. Final message: files, pytest result, the Granite summary table, gaps.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
